{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-178427-r4512935","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Indonesian-style Fried Rice","sourcePageId":178427,"sourceRevision":"4512935","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-06-18T23:49:29Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Indonesian-style%20Fried%20Rice&oldid=4512935","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:07:00.536Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Easy recipes","Category:Indonesian recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes using chicken","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using rice","Category:Recipes using vegetable oil","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"99446e8ac049beff821a3fbca9b300c2e73947b181ed9dfe88dbe691531cca6a","sourceWikitext":"__NOTOC__\n{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Rice recipes\n| Difficulty = 2\n}}\n\n{{recipe}}\n\n'''Indonesian-style fried rice''' is a popular food in Indonesia. \n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Fried rice ===\n* 5 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tablespoons]] [[Cookbook:Vegetable Oil|vegetable oil]]\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]], beaten\n* 3 cloves [[Cookbook:Garlic|garlic]], crushed\n* 3 red [[Cookbook:Chiles|chillies]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 100 [[Cookbook:Gram|grams]] [[Cookbook:Bean Sprout|beansprouts]], washed\n* 75 grams green peas, washed\n* 3 pieces [[Cookbook:Spring Onion|spring onion]], cut into 1 cm pieces\n* 150 grams [[Cookbook:Prawn|prawn]] or [[Cookbook:Chicken|chicken]], [[Cookbook:Dice|diced]]\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]] plain cooked white [[Cookbook:Rice|rice]]\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ¾ tsp [[Cookbook:Pepper|pepper]]\n* 2 tsp light [[Cookbook:Soy Sauce|soy sauce]]\n\n===Toppings===\n\n* 2 shrimp crackers\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] mixed pickles\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Fried Eggs|fried egg]], cooked sunny-side up\n* 10 pieces chicken satay\n* 1 fried chicken\n\n==Procedure==\n\n#Heat 2 tablespoons oil in a [[Cookbook:Frying Pan|pan]]. Add the beaten eggs, and cook, stirring until scrambled. Place it on the top of the rice. \n#Heat 3 tablespoons oil, add the garlic and red chillies, and [[Cookbook:Frying|fry]] until fragrant.\n#Add prawn or chicken to the pan, and cook until the color changes.\n#Add green peas, beansprouts, and spring onion. Add the rice and scrambled eggs, and cook for 5 minutes.\n#Add salt, pepper, and light soy sauce. Cook until the rice is softened.\n#Top the fried rice with the fried egg, fried chicken, mixed pickles, shrimp crackers, and chicken satay.\n#Divide into portions, and serve.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using rice]]\n[[Category:Indonesian recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using chicken]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Indonesian-style Fried Rice","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"5 tablespoons vegetable oil","sourceText":"5 tablespoons vegetable oil","amountText":"5 tablespoons vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"3 eggs, beaten","sourceText":"3 eggs, beaten","amountText":"3 eggs, beaten","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"so